---
layout: layout.njk
title: "Habibi — A little closer. A lot more private."
description: "Meet Habibi, an open-source personal AI companion in development. Local memory, your choice of AI provider, and encrypted sync designed to keep you in control."
pagination:
  data: locales
  size: 1
  alias: locale
permalink: "{{ locale | homePath }}"
---
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow status"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "An open-source companion, in the making") }}</p>
      <h1 id="hero-heading">
        <span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "A little closer.") }}</span>
        <span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "A lot more") }}</span>
        <span class="last-word">{{ dgettext("marketing", "private.") }}<svg class="headline-spark" viewBox="0 0 100 85" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m24 48 9-33m18 41 23-24m-13 48 25-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="11" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-intro">{{ dgettext("marketing", "A personal AI companion for the little things that make up a life. Built to remember what matters, without making your life someone else’s business.") }}</p>
      <p class="hero-detail">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Your memories on your devices. Your choice of AI provider.") }}<br class="desktop-break"> {{ dgettext("marketing", "A quieter kind of technology.") }}</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/pepicrft/habibi" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Explore on GitHub") }} {% include "arrow.njk" %}</a>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="{{ locale | homePath }}#about">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Meet Habibi") }} <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-preview" aria-labelledby="concept-caption">
      <div class="preview-stage">
        <div class="hello-companion">{% include "companion.njk" %}</div>
        <svg class="preview-doodle" viewBox="0 0 120 100" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 73c25 8 69-2 72-34 2-19-20-23-22-8-3 18 21 20 40 9m-1-12 5 14-15 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <span class="preview-aside" aria-hidden="true">Less to hold<br>in your head.</span>
        <div class="phone">
          <div class="phone-status" aria-hidden="true"><span>9:41</span><span class="phone-camera"></span><span>▮▮▮ <span class="battery"></span></span></div>
          <div class="phone-heading">{% include "companion.njk" %}<span>habibi</span><span class="phone-day">{{ dgettext("marketing", "a little everyday help") }}</span></div>
          <div class="conversation">
            <p class="conversation-date">{{ dgettext("marketing", "A SATURDAY, SOMEDAY") }}</p>
            <div class="memory-slip"><span class="memory-label"><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span> {{ dgettext("marketing", "A note you kept") }}</span><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Lunch with Maya.") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "She mentioned Olive & Fig.") }}</p></div>
            <p class="bubble bubble-you"><span class="visually-hidden">{{ dgettext("marketing", "You:") }} </span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "What was that little place Maya wanted to try?") }}</p>
            <div class="bubble bubble-habibi"><p><span class="visually-hidden">Habibi: </span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Olive & Fig. You saved it after your walk together.") }}</p><span class="memory-source">{{ dgettext("marketing", "From your own notes") }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div>
            <p class="bubble bubble-you bubble-last"><span class="visually-hidden">{{ dgettext("marketing", "You:") }} </span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "That’s the one. A little less to remember.") }}</p>
          </div>
          <p class="phone-note"><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span> {{ dgettext("marketing", "Little things, remembered.") }}</p>
          <div class="home-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </div>
        <span class="preview-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption id="concept-caption"><span class="caption-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "A glimpse of what we’re building") }}<br><span class="caption-detail">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Interface concept, not a released app.") }}</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section wrap section-space" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / {{ dgettext("marketing", "A little more human") }}</p>
      <h2 id="about-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "For a life.") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Not a user profile.") }}</h2>
      <p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Good company pays attention. It remembers the little things, helps you connect the dots, and leaves you room to be yourself. That’s the idea behind Habibi.") }}</p>
      <svg class="sprout" viewBox="0 0 180 130" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20 114c42-3 90-2 139 0M88 112V63m0 18C56 81 36 64 34 42c24-3 51 12 54 39Zm1-14c2-26 19-45 45-47-1 26-18 45-45 47Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="pillars">
      <article class="pillar"><span class="pillar-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Your life, in your hands.") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Habibi is being designed with memory and search on your devices. A place for your thoughts, plans, and everyday details, not a profile for advertisers.") }}</p></div></article>
      <article class="pillar"><span class="pillar-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Your companion. Your choice.") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Choose your inference provider and connect to it directly from the app. Habibi’s sync service won’t hold your provider credentials. The provider will see the context you send.") }}</p></div></article>
      <article class="pillar"><span class="pillar-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Open from the beginning.") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "No mystery about what’s being built. The code, decisions, and rough edges belong in the open, so you can look inside, ask questions, or make it your own.") }}</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="privacy-section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
    <div class="wrap privacy-inner">
      <div class="privacy-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / {{ dgettext("marketing", "Privacy, with the details left in") }}</p><h2 id="privacy-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Personal doesn’t have") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "to mean public.") }}</h2><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "“Private” should explain where your information goes.") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Here’s the design we’re working toward.") }}</p></div>
      <div class="data-flow" role="group" aria-label="{{ dgettext('marketing', 'Planned data flow') }}">
        <div class="flow-local"><span class="flow-tag">{{ dgettext("marketing", "STARTS WITH YOU") }}</span><svg class="device-icon" viewBox="0 0 52 62" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="10" y="3" width="32" height="54" rx="6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M22 9h8m-8 42h8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="m20 30 5 5 9-12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Your devices") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Memory, search, and the agent loop stay local. Your devices hold the vault key and encrypt content before sync.") }}</p><span class="flow-footnote">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Readable memories live here.") }}</span></div>
        <div class="flow-routes">
          <div class="flow-route"><div class="route-label"><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Selected context · direct from your device") }}</span></div><div class="flow-destination"><span class="flow-tag">{{ dgettext("marketing", "WHEN YOU USE AI") }}</span><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Your chosen provider") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "The provider receives selected prompts and context to generate a response. Its privacy and retention policies apply.") }}</p></div></div>
          <div class="flow-route"><div class="route-label"><span aria-hidden="true">↔</span><span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Encrypted content · optional device sync") }}</span></div><div class="flow-destination"><span class="flow-tag">{{ dgettext("marketing", "WHEN YOU SYNC") }}</span><h3>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Habibi’s sync service") }}</h3><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Ciphertext in object storage. No content keys or provider credentials. The service still sees account and sync metadata.") }}</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="privacy-bottom"><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Not a promise of invisibility. A clear boundary around who can read what.") }}</span></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="building-section wrap section-space" id="building" aria-labelledby="building-heading">
    <div class="build-copy"><p class="eyebrow">03 / {{ dgettext("marketing", "Early days, open doors") }}</p><h2 id="building-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Not quite in your pocket.") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Very much in the works.") }}</h2><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Habibi is a personal, open-source project in early development. The first piece is a ciphertext-only sync prototype. The mobile companion is still ahead.") }}</p><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "The plan is deliberately small: an Elixir backend, Postgres for a little metadata, and affordable S3-compatible storage for encrypted objects. Stateless sync servers that can grow without becoming a home for your readable memories.") }}</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/pepicrft/habibi" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Follow the work on GitHub") }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <aside class="build-note" aria-labelledby="build-note-heading"><span class="note-pin" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="eyebrow">{{ dgettext("marketing", "A note from the workbench") }}</p><h3 id="build-note-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Small steps.") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Clear intentions.") }}</h3><ul><li>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Local-first memory") }}</li><li>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Device-owned encryption keys") }}</li><li>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Direct-to-provider AI") }}</li><li>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Built in the open") }}</li></ul><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "A design direction, not an audited security guarantee.") }}</p><svg class="note-spark" viewBox="0 0 70 70" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m35 5 4 21 20-10-14 17 20 7-22 2 7 21-15-17-12 18 4-22-22-2 20-8L11 16l20 11Z" fill="currentColor"/></svg></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section wrap section-space" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">{{ dgettext("marketing", "A few good questions") }}</p><h2 id="faq-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Good to know.") }}</h2><p class="faq-aside">{{ dgettext("marketing", "No fine print.") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Just the important bits.") }}</p></div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details><summary>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Can my AI provider read my conversations?") }}<span class="details-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "It can read the prompts and selected context your device sends to it. The app is being designed to call your chosen provider directly, using credentials held on your device. Encryption for Habibi sync does not hide prompts from that provider. Its own privacy and retention policies apply.") }}</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>{{ dgettext("marketing", "What can Habibi’s sync service see?") }}<span class="details-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "The design keeps synced content encrypted with a random vault key owned by your devices. The service stores ciphertext, not readable memories, content keys, or inference-provider credentials. It still sees account and operational sync metadata, such as object sizes and when sync requests happen. This is not anonymity.") }}</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>{{ dgettext("marketing", "What happens if I lose my devices?") }}<span class="details-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Recovery requires both a recovery key you keep separately and an exported encrypted recovery bundle. The reference client can export encrypted recovery bundles; the mobile recovery interface isn’t built yet. Habibi’s operator won’t hold your vault key or recover your content for you. If you lose every device and either your recovery key or the encrypted bundle is unavailable, the operator cannot recover your content.") }}</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Can I download Habibi yet?") }}<span class="details-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Not yet. This is an early open-source project, starting with a ciphertext-only sync prototype, not a released mobile app. The interface above is a concept. There’s no launch date or waitlist; you can follow progress and explore the code on") }} <a href="https://github.com/pepicrft/habibi" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Does local-first mean the AI runs offline?") }}<span class="details-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "No. Local-first describes where memory, search, and the agent loop are intended to live. Using a remote inference provider requires a connection and sends selected context to that provider. There’s no planned silent fallback to a different remote provider.") }}</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing wrap" aria-labelledby="closing-heading"><div>{% include "companion.njk" %}<p class="eyebrow">{{ dgettext("marketing", "A small beginning") }}</p><h2 id="closing-heading">{{ dgettext("marketing", "A kinder corner") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "of your everyday.") }}</h2><a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/pepicrft/habibi" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ dgettext("marketing", "Come see what’s taking shape") }} {% include "arrow.njk" %}</a></div><p>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Open source.") }}<br>{{ dgettext("marketing", "Yours by design.") }}</p></section>
</main>
